SUMMARY:Math — There will be times when you will need to teach a concept
  on a ho...
DESCRIPTION:There will be times when you will need to teach a concept on a
  homeschool day. Today is one of those days! You will be teaching and ass
 essing knowledge for lesson 9. This lesson is a review on numbers 15 and 
 16. Your student may also need a reminder about how to read a pictograph.
  Important things to remember are to look at each row and write the numbe
 r of items at the end. Then you can go back and compare the information t
 o answer the questions. A review of odd vs even is also addressed on thes
 e pages. Complete pages 19 and 20 to determine if skills need more practi
 ce. I have included the review pages (17-18) for lesson 9 if your student
  needs extra practice today or before the Ch 2 test on Thursday.\n\nThere
  will be times when you will need to teach a concept on a homeschool day.
  Today is one of those days! You will be teaching and assessing knowledge
  for lesson 9. This lesson is a review on numbers 15 and 16. Your student
  may also need a reminder about how to read a pictograph. Important thing
 s to remember are to look at each row and write the number of items at th
 e end. Then you can go back and compare the information to answer the que
 stions. A review of odd vs even is also addressed on these pages. Complet
 e pages 19 and 20 to determine if skills need more practice. I have inclu
 ded the review pages (17-18) for lesson 9 if your student needs extra pra
 ctice today or before the Ch 2 test on Thursday.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
