UID:HW265904-2026-09-02-lilyanne@facts-split
DTSTAMP:20260806T002149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260903
SUMMARY:Math — Complete p. 29-32 in their math worktext. For page 31: Us
 e the gr...
DESCRIPTION:Complete p. 29-32 in their math worktext. For page 31: Use the
  graphic at the top of the page to act out different plans to put plants 
 in the picnic area. Create word problems such as- If DQ wants to put 5 fl
 ower pots along the fence and Liam wants to put 1 pot near the picnic tab
 le. How many will they need in all? You can use any object to represent t
 he pots or have your student draw them. Complete p. 1 in Math Fact Review
  Folder We will be starting Fact Reviews this week. You will find this ye
 llow folder in their backpacks. The objective of the math fact reviews is
  to master/memorize simple math facts in order to solidify the student's 
 foundation of math\, making other skills easier and quicker. Instructions
  for Fact Review Pages: Give your student 2 minutes to complete all 20 ma
 th facts on the page. When the timer goes off-circle the facts that are i
 ncomplete or incorrect. Then have your student go back and complete the c
 ircled facts. This helps me understand and assess their growth. We will t
 urn in the Math Fact Folders once a term for a grade. In addition to the 
 reviews done at home\, we will do Math Fact Reviews in class using this s
 ame method and your student will receive a grade. Guide completion of Dai
 ly Math Week 4 day 2.\n\nComplete p. 29-32 in their math worktext. For pa
 ge 31: Use the graphic at the top of the page to act out different plans 
 to put plants in the picnic area. Create word problems such as- If DQ wan
 ts to put 5 flower pots along the fence and Liam wants to put 1 pot near 
 the picnic table. How many will they need in all? You can use any object 
 to represent the pots or have your student draw them. Complete p. 1 in Ma
 th Fact Review Folder We will be starting Fact Reviews this week. You wil
 l find this yellow folder in their backpacks. The objective of the math f
 act reviews is to master/memorize simple math facts in order to solidify 
 the student's foundation of math\, making other skills easier and quicker
 . Instructions for Fact Review Pages: Give your student 2 minutes to comp
 lete all 20 math facts on the page. When the timer goes off-circle the fa
 cts that are incomplete or incorrect. Then have your student go back and 
 complete the circled facts. This helps me understand and assess their gro
 wth. We will turn in the Math Fact Folders once a term for a grade. In ad
 dition to the reviews done at home\, we will do Math Fact Reviews in clas
 s using this same method and your student will receive a grade. Guide com
 pletion of Daily Math Week 4 day 2.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
